%% DM26-0670

sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant D as Domain actor
    participant F as Facade + Outbox
    participant T as Transport
    participant B as Broker

    D->>F: Publish(topic, payload)
    F->>F: assign (epoch, seq) and append to the outbox
    F->>T: Send(PublishRequest, epoch, seq)
    T->>B: PublishRequest(epoch, seq)
    B->>B: at the session ingress, in socket order: already accepted? acknowledge again. Pending? wait. New? hand to the topic actor
    B->>B: the topic actor accepts it
    B-->>T: PublishRequestAck(epoch, seq), for this message only
    T-->>F: Acked(epoch, seq)
    F->>F: remove exactly that entry from the outbox
    F-->>D: PublishAcknowledged (optional receipt)
    Note over F,B: A message leaves the outbox only when the broker acknowledges that exact message.<br/>Acks can come back in any order, because different topic actors answer.<br/>Writing it to the socket proves nothing.
